<title>TURKEY: TURK FINANSBANK LAUNCHES $30-MLN SYNDICATED LOAN.</title>
<headline>TURK FINANSBANK LAUNCHES $30-MLN SYNDICATED LOAN.</headline>
<dateline>ANKARA 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Turkey's Finansbank launched a $30 million syndicated loan on Thursday, a bank official said.</p>
<p>The official said the one-year pre-export financing facility, arranged by Standard Chartered, Sakura and West LB, will have an interest of LIBOR plus 90 basis points.</p>
</text>
